# Working Principle

1. The INMP441 continuously captures audio.
2. ESP32 receives the audio through I2S.
3. Audio is divided into processing frames.
4. MFCC features are extracted.
5. The lightweight CNN processes the MFCC features.
6. The model determines whether the audio contains ASTHRA.
7. If ASTHRA is not detected, the device continues listening.
8. If ASTHRA is detected, speech recording is activated.
9. Recorded speech is transmitted to the ASR server.
10. The ASR server converts speech into text.
11. The OLED provides device status information.